Rationale: The evidence collectively supports all material parts of the claim. The home of the race is confirmed as Circuit Gilles Villeneuve in Montreal, Quebec, which is also the venue for the FIA Formula One Canadian Grand Prix. The first Formula One race won by a black driver occurred at this venue in 1978. The evidence also confirms that Canadian drivers Jacques Villeneuve and Lance Stroll participated in the Canadian Grand Prix since 2006.
